{"title":"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Tangential_Distance)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2  (Tangential Distance)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_(With_Animation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution (With Animation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A flat board has a circular hole with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a circular hole with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that the distance between the centers of the two holes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17ce6fcb2994d4241d780dd5311d828db133411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> Two spheres with equal radii sit in the two holes such that the spheres are tangent to each other. The square of the radius of the spheres is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c80f7cbc6e8017ab735d473c6f3eb2e66a40511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3493ac92ddd157a54c88f53fdb25d258a5f123.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(300); import graph3; import solids;  currentprojection=orthographic((1,-5,1)); real r = sqrt(160/13);  triple C1, C2, B1, B2; C1 = (0,0,sqrt(r^2-1^2)); C2 = (7,0,sqrt(r^2-2^2)); B1 = (0,0,0); B2 = (7,0,0); draw((-5,-10,0)--(-5,10,0)--(12,10,0)--(12,-10,0)--cycle); draw(shift(C1)*scale3(r)*unitsphere,yellow,light=White); draw(shift(C2)*scale3(r)*unitsphere,yellow,light=White); draw(Circle(B1,1,(0,0,1))); draw(Circle(B2,2,(0,0,1)));  dot(C1^^C2^^B1^^B2,linewidth(4.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"225\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pythagorean_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pythagorean_Theorem)\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pythagorean Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63af3ee78c8a31a2ef396006676d018ab50a0d2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(10cm); pair A, B, C, D, O, P, H, L, X, Y; A = (-1, 0); B = (1, 0); H = (0, 0); C = (5, 0); D = (9, 0); L = (7, 0); O = (0, sqrt(160/13 - 1)); P = (7, sqrt(160/13 - 4)); X = (0, sqrt(160/13 - 4)); Y = (O + P) / 2;  draw(A -- O -- B -- cycle); draw(C -- P -- D -- cycle); draw(B -- C); draw(O -- P); draw(P -- X, dashed); draw(O -- H, dashed); draw(P -- L, dashed);  draw(circle(O, sqrt(160/13))); draw(circle(P, sqrt(160/13))); path b = brace(L-(0,1), H-(0,1),0.5); draw(b);  label(&quot;$r$&quot;, O -- Y, N); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, Y -- P, N); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, O -- A, NW); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, P -- D, NE); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, A -- H, N); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, L -- D, N); label(&quot;$7$&quot;, b, S);  dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^O^^P^^H^^L^^X^^Y,linewidth(4)); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"305\" />\nSet the common radius to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. First, take the cross section of the sphere sitting in the hole of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If we draw the perpendicular bisector of the chord (the hole) through the circle, this line goes through the center. Connect the center also to where the chord hits the circle, for a right triangle with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the height of this circle outside of the hole is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b162b52a624076f304ee4a250639394cda413a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{r^2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The other circle follows similarly for a height (outside the hole) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aaa9f6788ce44bec07b0a8d5e87dec1c71f9a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{r^2-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. Now, if we take the cross section of the entire board, essentially making it two-dimensional, we can connect the centers of the two spheres, then form another right triangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as given by the problem. The height of this triangle is the difference between the heights of the parts of the two spheres outside the holes, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c41bc5747b9f89f6614fa0e61c46b015fcba43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{r^2-1} - \\sqrt{r^2-4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />. Now we can set up an equation in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with the Pythagorean theorem: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5333012aea3a045a0d96d846d94552e32c9970f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sqrt{r^2-1} - \\sqrt{r^2-4}\\right)^2 + 7^2 = (2r)^2.\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"35\" /> Simplifying a few times,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b553d8959ce1fd77b4c802aafa8a200e964b5fdb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} r^2 - 1 - 2\\left(\\sqrt{(r^2-1)(r^2-4)}\\right) + r^2 - 4 + 49 &amp;= 4r^2 \\\\ 2r^2-44 &amp;= -2\\left(\\sqrt{(r^2-1)(r^2-4)}\\right) \\\\ 22-r^2 &amp;= \\left(\\sqrt{r^4 - 5r^2 + 4}\\right) \\\\ r^4 -44r^2 + 484 &amp;= r^4 - 5r^2 + 4 \\\\ 39r^2&amp;=480 \\\\ r^2&amp;=\\frac{480}{39} = \\frac{160}{13}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"572\" height=\"229\" />\nTherefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/952cf60fbe678f4ff0dc12dae6e235b9e33ca121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{173}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~molocyxu\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Tangential_Distance.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Tangential_Distance)\">Solution 2  (Tangential Distance)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2  (Tangential Distance)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AIME_I_6a.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bb/2020_AIME_I_6a.png/400px-2020_AIME_I_6a.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"161\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bb/2020_AIME_I_6a.png/600px-2020_AIME_I_6a.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bb/2020_AIME_I_6a.png/800px-2020_AIME_I_6a.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the centers of the holes, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of crossing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and  radical axes of the circles. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has equal tangential distance to any point of both spheres. In particular to the circles (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_axis\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radical_axis</a>.)\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AIME_I_6d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c3/2020_AIME_I_6d.png/400px-2020_AIME_I_6d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"284\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c3/2020_AIME_I_6d.png/600px-2020_AIME_I_6d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c3/2020_AIME_I_6d.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a025b6d15152ebff4c98d5477dc438c4de6ac452.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CA = \\frac {AB} {2} – \\frac {r_A^2 – r_B^2}{2 AB} = \\frac{23}{7}, CB = AB - AC =\\frac{26}{7},\\]\" width=\"382\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/993874475cb03305ed2d842324e51b338cbf88cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CA&#39; = CB&#39;= \\sqrt{BC^2 – r_B^2} = \\frac {4}{7} \\sqrt{30}.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of tangency of the spheres common radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c015d9b401e93019cc959ddce44b3250e8f741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O&#39;.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the angle between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a84f8f3319f3db47689ce8470b564da9fddf0522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OO&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and flat board. In the plane, perpendicular to board <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad361428d6c5f4abbe1b74d7a1b7ec2bd0f7121e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DC \\perp OO&#39;, DC =  \\frac {4}{7} \\sqrt{30}.\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AIME_I_6b.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/44/2020_AIME_I_6b.png/400px-2020_AIME_I_6b.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"214\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/44/2020_AIME_I_6b.png/600px-2020_AIME_I_6b.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/4/44/2020_AIME_I_6b.png/800px-2020_AIME_I_6b.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4eafc0d42cea197297ba90816d5380a94bee11d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = \\frac {26}{7} - \\frac {7}{2} = \\frac{3}{14} \\implies \\sin \\alpha = \\frac {d}{DC} = \\frac {3}{8\\sqrt {30}}.\\]\" width=\"356\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af1c1835b358527f286f2f3d1956839c1a6878c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos \\alpha = \\sqrt {1 – \\frac {9}{64 \\cdot 30}} = \\sqrt{ \\frac {637}{640}} = \\frac {7}{2} \\sqrt {\\frac{13}{160}}.\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3b4ac08893261aaa785d9dfa52759e05f997cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2R \\cos \\alpha = AB = 7 \\implies R = \\frac {\\frac{7}{2} } {\\frac{7}{2}\\sqrt \\frac{13}{160}} = \\sqrt {\\frac{160}{13}}.\\]\" width=\"371\" height=\"59\" />\nHence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/8/1682b40611ee785e009d92b915f30d6753abfb88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[160+13 = \\boxed{173}.\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"23\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_solution_.28With_Animation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_(With_Animation)\">Video solution (With Animation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution (With Animation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cOf9uTJ9J40\">https://youtu.be/cOf9uTJ9J40</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qCTq8KhZfYQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qCTq8KhZfYQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I\" title=\"2020 AIME I\">2020 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?tit